diff --git a/features/todo-completion.feature b/features/todo-completion.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ea439e1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-completion.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+Feature: Todo completion and item editing
+  As a todo-list user
+  I want to complete, toggle, and edit my todos
+  So that I can manage each item's state
+
+  Scenario: Completing a single todo toggles its completed state
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a"
+    When I complete the todo "a"
+    Then the todo "a" shows the completed state
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all control completes every todo
+    Given the app loads with active todos "a" and "b"
+    When I click the toggle-all control
+    Then every todo item shows the completed state
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all control clears every todo
+    Given the app loads with completed todos "a" and "b"
+    When I click the toggle-all control
+    Then every todo item shows the active state
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all control reflects full completion
+    Given the app loads with active todos "a" and "b"
+    When I complete the todo "a"
+    And I complete the todo "b"
+    Then the toggle-all control is checked
+
+  Scenario: Each todo item exposes a destroy control
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    Then the todo "a" has a destroy control
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label enters edit mode
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
+    Then the todo "a" is in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on Enter and leaves edit mode
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
+    And I set the edit input to "Buy a unicorn" and press Enter
+    Then the todo "a" shows title "Buy a unicorn"
+    And the todo "a" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on blur and leaves edit mode
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
+    And I set the edit input to "Buy a unicorn" and blur
+    Then the todo "a" shows title "Buy a unicorn"
+    And the todo "a" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing to empty destroys the todo
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
+    And I set the edit input to "   " and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows no items
+
+  Scenario: Escape cancels the edit and discards changes
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
+    And I set the edit input to "changed" and press Escape
+    Then the todo "a" shows title "a"
+    And the todo "a" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/todo-creation.feature b/features/todo-creation.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fb137e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-creation.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Todo creation and display
+  As a todo-list user
+  I want to add todos and see my list and remaining count
+  So that I can track what needs doing
+
+  Scenario: An empty list hides the main section and footer
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: The new-todo input is focused on load
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    Then the new-todo input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Entering a title adds a todo and clears the input
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows one item with title "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only input creates no todo
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When I type "   " into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows no items
+
+  Scenario: The counter shows the active count with correct pluralization
+    Given the app loads with active todos "a" and "b" and completed todo "c"
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter singularizes one active item
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a" and completed todo "b"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: The counter shows zero items
+    Given the app loads with completed todo "a"
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
diff --git a/features/todo-filtering.feature b/features/todo-filtering.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..176cf3b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-filtering.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Todo filtering, routing, and clearing
+  As a todo-list user
+  I want to filter my list and clear finished work
+  So that I can focus on what remains
+
+  Scenario: The clear-completed button removes completed todos
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a" and completed todo "b"
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list shows one item with title "a"
+
+  Scenario: The clear-completed button is hidden with no completed todos
+    Given the app loads with active todos "a" and "b"
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed todos hides and unchecks the toggle-all control
+    Given the app loads with completed todos "a" and "b"
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list shows no items
+    And the toggle-all control is unchecked
+    And the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: The All filter shows every todo
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a" and completed todo "b"
+    When I open the "All" filter
+    Then the todo list shows two items
+    And the "All" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The Active filter hides completed todos
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a" and completed todo "b"
+    When I open the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo list shows one item with title "a"
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The Completed filter hides active todos
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a" and completed todo "b"
+    When I open the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo list shows one item with title "b"
+    And the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: An item completed in a filtered view updates immediately
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a" and completed todo "b"
+    When I open the "Active" filter
+    And I complete the todo "a"
+    Then the todo list shows no items
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists across a reload
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a" and completed todo "b"
+    When I open the "Completed" filter
+    And I reload the app
+    Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+    And the todo list shows one item with title "b"
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ab91d84
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a todo-list user
+  I want my todos to survive a page reload
+  So that I do not lose my list
+
+  Rule: The app stores todos under the localStorage key "todos-vanillajs"
+
+  Scenario: Adding a todo persists it to localStorage
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains a todo with title "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo persists the completed state
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a"
+    When I complete the todo "a"
+    Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" marks the todo "a" as completed
+
+  Scenario: Each stored todo carries the id, title, and completed fields
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then every stored todo under "todos-vanillajs" has the keys "id", "title", and "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
+    Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" records no editing state for the todo "a"
